bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    mir_enum_payload_inline_none_lowered_as_nil_2026-11-10, 0, "Phase-3 stage3 build (stage2_new4.exe) rejects inline `None` in a declared `T?` enum payload slot as a NilLit: MirInstKind.Call(None, ...) at string_builder_opt.spl:197:71 (also HirTypeKind.Array/HirExprKind.IntLit sites). The HIR node at the None span reaches MIR as HirExprKind.NilLit; pure-Simple lowering and minimal stage2 builds admit the same shapes, so the defect is in the stage2-native path, root cause not yet located."

bugs |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    mir_enum_payload_inline_none_lowered_as_nil_2026-11-10, P1, open, "stage2 native: inline None payload arg reaches MIR as NilLit, rejected as nil outside unsafe", src/compiler/60.mir_opt/mir_opt/string_builder_opt.spl, 197, test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/enum_payload_inline_none_contexts_spec.spl, 2026-11-10, 2026-11-10, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    mir_enum_payload_inline_none_lowered_as_nil_2026-11-10, 0, "2026-11-10: NOT reproduced. Interpreter MIR spec (direct, struct-field, if-val arm in while, match arm) all admit None; stage2_new4.exe native-build of 1- and 2-module repros of the exact string_builder_opt shape links and runs. Source review: no frontend/HIR/codec path rewrites None to NilLit (HIR emits NamedVar; codec round-trips NamedVar). Entry-closure stage2 build of string_builder_opt crashed in MIR shard (invalid array handle) before reaching it. Next: capture the stage3 HIR shard for compiler.mir_opt.string_builder_opt and decode the arg node. Call-site workaround lane is separate."
